# mysanity runs fully single-player with no environment variables.
# Journal entries and mood check-ins are never sent to a server.
#
# Optional Postgres, for accounts, cloud saves, and the shared town.
# Leave DATABASE_URL unset and the game never tries to connect.
#
# Railway: open your Postgres service → Variables → copy DATABASE_PUBLIC_URL
# (the public URL, not the internal railway.internal one).
# Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables → add
#   DATABASE_URL = that public URL
# for Production, Preview and Development, then redeploy.
#
# Apply the schema before the first deploy that should use the database:
#   DATABASE_URL="postgresql://..." npm run db:migrate
# You can run that from your laptop, from Railway's shell, or from any
# machine that can reach the public URL. Vercel does not run it for you.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:port/railway
#
# Review key for business boards. Make up a long random string (16+ characters)
# and put the same value in Vercel as ADMIN_TOKEN. Do not commit the real value.
# The owner pastes it into /admin/boards to approve or reject submissions.
# ADMIN_TOKEN=

# Leave this unset while testing. The site tells search engines NOT to index it.
# Set to 1 only when you are ready to launch publicly (after clinical review), then redeploy.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOW_INDEXING=1
